  "version": "0.20.0",
  "language": "eng",
  "description": "<p><strong>MontuPython</strong> (<em>mnṯw ꜥꜣpp(y)</em>) is a Python package to compute astronomical ephemerides in the ancient world — thousands of years before the present. It was developed for ancient Egypt and applies equally to other sites of cultural and archaeoastronomical interest.</p><p>Version 0.20.0 adds <strong>MontuPython Desktop</strong> (PySide6 GUI), refactored example notebooks, expanded tests, and several API fixes in the stellar catalogue and observer utilities. See <code>WHATSNEW.md</code> in the repository for full release notes.</p><p>Ephemeris calculations rely primarily on <a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/ephem/\">PyEphem</a>, with support from <a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/pymeeus/\">PyMeeus</a>, <a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/spiceypy/\">spiceypy</a>, and <a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/pyplanets/\">pyplanets</a>.</p>",
